   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ שְׁנַיִם שֶׁהוֹצִיאוּ שְׁטַר חוֹב זֶה עַל זֶה, אַדְמוֹן אוֹמֵר: אִילּוּ הָיִיתִי חַיָּיב לְךָ — כֵּיצַד אַתָּה לֹוֶה מִמֶּנִּי?! וַחֲכָמִים אוֹמְרִים: זֶה גּוֹבֶה שְׁטַר חוֹבוֹ, וְזֶה גּוֹבֶה שְׁטַר חוֹבוֹ.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» With regard to «two» people «who» each «produced a promissory note» of a monetary debt «against the other, Admon says:» The one holding the note with the later date can say to the first: «If I owed you» money, «how» is it that «you are borrowing from me?» You should have sued to collect your debt. This is proof that your document is a forgery. «And the Rabbis say: This one collects his promissory note, and that one collects his promissory note.»"
  }
 ],
